@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
title Resumefolio | Requirements change management
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
 BorderColor #64748B
 FontColor #17324D
 DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
 DiamondBorderColor #B45309
 StartColor #17324D
 EndColor #17324D
}
start
:Record requested change, reason, source and current revision;
:Distinguish routine correction from changed meaning / commitment;
:Trace affected records, dependencies, evidence and consequences;
if (New owner decision required?) then (yes)
 :Present options, recommendation and remaining uncertainty; <<#FEF3C7>>
 if (Actual decision authorizes the proposed update?) then (yes)
  :Record decision, rationale, revision and conditions;
 else (rejected / deferred / pending)
  :Retain actual outcome or pending status and reasons; <<#FEF3C7>>
  :Keep proposal unapplied; record owner, next action and gate;
  stop
 endif
else (within existing authority)
 :Proceed within accepted meaning and existing authorization;
endif
:Update authoritative text, criteria, models, definitions and links; <<#DCFCE7>>
:Re-review affected content and evidence applicability;
if (Relevant checks and review complete?) then (yes)
 :Preserve focused revision and actual review outcome;
else (not yet)
 :Record findings and keep dependent acceptance unresolved; <<#FEF3C7>>
endif
:Update baseline references only through an actual baseline decision;
stop
legend bottom
Requirement state, delivery state and verification result are distinct.
Accepted snapshots remain retrievable; a new commit alone is not acceptance.
Material scope, spending and delivery changes require an explicit owner decision.
endlegend
@enduml
